  "id": "ai-context/a-content-without-text-reads-in-later-history-as-its-turn-read-it",
  "title": "A location, a template, a composite holding them, a voice message and a video read in a model's later history as the turn they started read them, their text form, whether the model sees or not",
  "rules": [
    "§6.4",
    "§6.6"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "RK-6.6-010",
    "RK-6.6-011",
    "RK-6.6-012",
    "RK-6.6-014",
    "RK-6.6-022",
    "RK-6.6-023",
    "RK-6.6-025",
    "RK-6.6-026"
  ],
  "notes": "RFC §6.6, Text form: a turn's history and input read a content as text by its text form; §6.4: the event a turn answers reads as the same event does in its history. The event a turn answers reaches the AI channel transcoded to that text, while the history reads the stored event: Python's _ai_context.py _read_as_text reads a location and a template there by their text form, as _media.py text_form writes it. Room 1's model does not see; room 2's sees, and reads a composite in its history part by part, the location its text form among them. A composite nested in a composite reads by its parts too (RMK-1743).",
